      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The valley’s early settlers were Dutch farmers in the mid‑1700s, drawn by fertile soil and waterways for milling.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/walker_valley_new_york",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Indigenous Lenape people inhabited the area for millennia, using the valley for hunting and seasonal villages until the late 1700s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/walker_valley_new_york",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Walker Valley sits on NY 52 where the road begins to climb the eastern slope of the Shawangunk Ridge.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11,
        14
